iption":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-03T23:28:27Z","updated_at":"2025-03-04T14:07:07Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.3 and 4.4 stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nVisual Shader node TextureParameterTriplanar produces incorrect normals. StandardMaterial3D works as expected. Triplanar normal calculations have been fixed [for standard material](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/82311) at some point, but doesn't seem like those changes have been implemented for the visual shader.\n\nFirst cube with visual triplanar, second is standard.\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eff00acb-2769-457e-8445-7a13b6ed398d)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a new visual shader with TextureParameterTriplanar, change its type to NomalMap and plug it into shader NormalMap input. Assign a new NoiseTexture2D, set its mode As Normal Map. \n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee steps to reproduce.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103534/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103534/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}